The mrsd parameter is indeed design for modern data.

For your issue, you can just plot the tree like other ordinary tree. Don’t confuse with time or substitution rate scale. Technically, they are the same and are all numeric values along the x-axis. Maybe what you want is just https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/87.

> Also, I managed to plot the age ranges with geom_range. When I open the function, it shows me the option of plotting the ages with plot_age which I suppose could plot the "height_median" information on the nodes. However, when I run it with this parameter, R says "Ignoring unknown parameters: plot_age". Also couldn't find it in the manual. What would be the best way to plot a text or numerical attribute on the nodes?
>

There is indeed no plot_age parameter.

